{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104232","id":2396073047,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6O0SxX","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/104232.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104232","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104232/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/104232/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/104232/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/54685c3037116b25093a4ab2b91e3b978dd0e06f","number":104232,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Deactivate the `CameraServer` by default.","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"I profiled the launch of tps demo. I noticed that launching the `CameraServer` took 12% (120ms) of the total CPU time (on macOS). I found this curious because tps-demo should not access my camera. \r\n\r\nI propose deactivating the `CameraServer` by default. I think this is appropriate for most games: Most do not need to monitor cameras, and monitoring the feeds as a game that does not use cameras is questionable at best.\r\n\r\nThe `CameraServer` can be activated in games that need it with `set_is_monitoring_feeds`, and queried with `is_monitoring_feeds`. \r\nMost games will not activate monitoring and thus won't pay for it. For games that do need the camera, I think it is still appropriate to be able to activate and deactive feed monitoring, because they may not need to monitor the feeds all the time.\r\n\r\n## Notes\r\n\r\nThis PR should be tested on Linux before merging. It should also be tested if the changes break camera monitoring, because I have no project to conveniently test it with.\r\n\r\nIt's also likely this PR (in its current state) will cause problems with the Godot editor itself, which may want to monitor feeds for editor purposes. I'm open to suggestions for where / how to support that.\r\n\r\nThis PR is a breaking change to games that use the camera feed. When they update, they'll need to start activating the server somewhere in their code.\r\n\r\n## Profiling\r\nI profiled tps demo and found it to launch 8% (0.14s) faster on average on macOS:\r\n```\r\nBenchmark 1: bin/godot.macos.editor.arm64.master --path /Users/lukas/dev/godot/tps-demo --quit\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):      1.772 s ±  0.034 s    [User: 0.597 s, System: 0.224 s]\r\n  Range (min … max):    1.710 s …  1.859 s    25 runs\r\n\r\nBenchmark 2: bin/godot.macos.editor.arm64 --path /Users/lukas/dev/godot/tps-demo --quit\r\n  Time (mean ± σ):      1.635 s ±  0.041 s    [User: 0.558 s, System: 0.168 s]\r\n  Range (min … max):    1.537 s …  1.715 s    25 runs\r\n\r\nSummary\r\n  bin/godot.macos.editor.arm64 --path /Users/lukas/dev/godot/tps-demo --quit ran\r\n    1.08 ± 0.03 times faster than bin/godot.macos.editor.arm64.master --path /Users/lukas/dev/godot/tps-demo --quit\r\n``` \r\n\r\nLinux uses an asynchronous approach to monitoring feeds, so it should benefit asynchronously instead of on launch time.\r\nWindows does not benefit because `CameraServer` is not implemented for it.\r\n\r\n## Addendum\r\nIt may be appropriate to move the `CameraServer` to a GDExtension because it is very self-contained, and it is questionable that code to monitor cameras even ships with all Godot games in the first place.\r\nHowever, this is out of scope for this PR, and likely won't provide much more tangible benefit than what is suggested here (as the camera module is very small).","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279097162,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTcxNjI=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/discussion","name":"discussion","description":"","color":"ccaaff","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":865585000,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4NjU1ODUwMDA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:xr","name":"topic:xr","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":12070367,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AuC3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/22","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/22/labels","number":22,"state":"closed","title":"4.5","description":"","creator":{"login":"Sauermann","id":6299227,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyOTkyMjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6299227?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Sauermann","html_url":"https://github.com/Sauerm